     "@type": "Question",
     "name": "Why is my peace lily drooping?",
     "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "A drooping peace lily is usually thirsty: UF/IFAS names underwatering as the most common problem, and a dry peace lily can wilt right down to the soil. Waterlogged soil can also make the leaves wilt, so feel the soil before you water."
     }
